{"t_ms": 8326640, "conversation_id": "conv_immediate_s2_015", "turn_id": 1, "actor": "system", "event_type": "retrieval_result", "payload": {"passages": ["Housekeeping Schedule\n\nGrand Horizon Hotel & Suites\n\nDaily housekeeping services are provided between 9:00 AM and 5:00 PM. Guests who prefer not to be disturbed may activate the \"Do Not Disturb\" indicator outside their room. Additional cleaning requests or replenishment of towels and toiletries can be made by contacting housekeeping through the in-room telephone.", "Dry Cleaning Service\n\nGrand Horizon Hotel & Suites\n\nProfessional dry cleaning services are available for delicate garments such as suits, dresses, and formal wear. Clothing collected before 10:00 AM is generally returned by the following evening. Charges vary depending on the garment type and are added to the guest's final bill.", "# corpus/ \u2014 Hotel Documents\n\n**Owner: Lakshya**\n\n## What this folder is\n\nThe hotel's documents live here: the knowledge the assistant answers from. About 60 short \ndocuments covering things like pool and gym hours, check-in and check-out rules, menus, and \npolicies.\n\n## How to fill it\n\nSee the full instructions in `retrieval/README.md` (Step 1). In short:\n- Write ~60 short documents, one topic per file, as `.txt` or `.md`.\n- Make them realistic and varied.\n- Deliberately plant a few contradictions (e.g. one doc says the pool closes at 10 PM, \n  another says 9 PM) and keep a note of which ones, for a later experiment.\n\nThe index-building script reads every file in this folder, so anything you put here becomes \npart of the searchable knowledge.\n"], "scores": [0.5362576842308044, 0.7265481948852539, 0.7410706281661987], "filenames": ["15_housekeeping.txt", "42_dry_cleaning.txt", "README.md"], "timing_policy": "immediate", "timing_trigger": "immediate", "user_end_known_at_finish": true, "launch_offset_ms_vs_user_end": 87, "overlap_with_speech_ms": 0, "forecast_invalidated": false}}
